{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"While rotating /rebar/prod/anthropic-api-key and re-materializing the container .env, a manual `docker compose up -d --force-recreate review-bot opcert mcp` on i-00880b2c7f13527c5 RACED the `rebar-autodeploy.timer` (which runs `docker compose` every ~2 min). The concurrent compose runs produced `Error response from daemon: No such container: <id>` and the manual `up` aborted partway, transiently leaving review-bot/opcert/mcp created-but-not-started (only gerrit up) — a self-inflicted ~1-2 min outage of the code-review bot, op-cert gate, and MCP server.\n\nRecovery that worked: `systemctl disable --now rebar-autodeploy.timer` → `docker compose up -d` → verify ps + `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` length in each consumer → `systemctl enable --now rebar-autodeploy.timer`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md secret-rotation / targeted-restart section documents the autodeploy-timer race and prescribes pausing `rebar-autodeploy.timer` for the recreate window (disable --now → up -d → re-enable --now), OR an equivalent lock so a manual compose op and the autodeploy tick cannot run concurrently.\n- [x] The `docker compose up -d --force-recreate <svc>` examples in that runbook cross-reference the pause step.\n\nNon-goals: changing autodeploy's cadence or adding a compose-level lock in autodeploy.sh itself (a heavier design change — file separately if wanted). This is a documentation/procedure fix.\n\n## Verification\n- Inspect `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` to confirm the secret-rotation/targeted-restart procedure explicitly pauses `rebar-autodeploy.timer` or an equivalent lock before manual compose recreates.\n- Run `env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_2 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_2 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` before Gerrit push and land the documentation change through Gerrit.\n\n\n## Implementation Plan\n- Edit only `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md`.\n- Add an operator procedure warning that any manual `docker compose up -d --force-recreate ...` in the review-bot/opcert/MCP stack must first pause `rebar-autodeploy.timer`, then run compose, verify containers are up, and finally re-enable the timer.\n- Cross-reference that pause procedure from existing force-recreate examples instead of changing autodeploy cadence or adding a new lock.\n- If the existing runbook lacks a clearly matching targeted-restart section, add a small subsection near the secret-rotation procedure and link the examples to it.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788773470492920001,"uuid":"8d50f177-c46a-4cea-bf54-d2c2ca7e07a4"}